// "PowerAndToughnessDown" = the debuff twin of `PowerAndToughnessUp`
// ([CR#613.4c] layer 7c): a single `Modification`-kind macro standing in a
// `changes: [...]` slot that expands to the -N/-M power-and-toughness debuff
// written inline as `[Power(Down(N)), Toughness(Down(M))]`. Delegates to the
// arity-2 `PowerAndToughness(NumericOp, NumericOp)` building block, forwarding
// its own params as `Down(Param(0))`/`Down(Param(1))` — a nested-macro
// param-forwarding mechanism. Usage: PowerAndToughnessDown(p, t)
// — e.g. PowerAndToughnessDown(2, 2) for a symmetric "-2/-2" debuff.
//
// Both params are a `Count`. Mixed "+N/-M" has no bundling macro — the
// emitter keeps the inline pair for that case.
(
    name: "PowerAndToughnessDown",
    template: "gets -${0}/-${1}",
    kinds: [Modification],
    params: [Count, Count],
    body: PowerAndToughness(Down(Param(0)), Down(Param(1))),
)
